---
const {kind="privacy"}=Astro.props;
const pages={
 privacy:{title:"Privacy, in plain terms.",intro:"This notice describes the information collected by the project inquiry service and how it is handled.",sections:[
  ["information","What you send","The inquiry form collects your name, an email address or phone number, and your country or delivery destination. Company, application, quantity, pole dimensions, foundation notes, project notes and an attachment are optional. Provide only what is useful for the request; avoid unrelated personal or confidential information."],
  ["purpose","Why it is collected","The information is used to understand your request, review a project configuration, respond through the contact channel you provide and keep a record of the correspondence. Distributor, support and privacy requests use the same inquiry service with the selected purpose recorded."],
  ["attachments","Drawings and attachments","An optional PDF, JPG or PNG of up to 5 MB can be submitted with the form. Attachments are held with the inquiry in the private inbox. They are not published on product pages or exposed through public download links. Avoid sending documents you are not authorised to share."],
  ["access","Storage and access","Requests are stored in a private inquiry database. The inbox, record details, attachments and export functions require a private operator access key. An on-page receipt confirms that the request was recorded; it does not mean an email notification was sent. External email notification and direct business contact channels are not yet configured."],
  ["site-data","Site and browser data","The core procurement pages use local site assets and do not include an advertising or third-party analytics integration. The inquiry record can include the page, language and limited campaign labels used to reach the form. Personal form content is not sent as an analytics event. Operational protection uses a temporary request-rate counter; it is not added to the inquiry record."],
  ["calculator","Cost scenario data","Calculator inputs are processed in the page. Calculating alone does not send them to the inquiry service or store a scenario. If you choose to carry a scenario into an inquiry, its notes are held temporarily in this browser tab, accepted for up to thirty minutes and removed from that storage when the quote form reads them. Review or edit the notes before submission. Only a submitted inquiry stores those notes with the request; financial values are not included in the calculator analytics event."],
  ["retention","Retention and requests","The operator should retain project correspondence only while it is needed for the request and related business records. A production retention schedule and corporate contact identity still need to be confirmed before public deployment. To ask about access, correction or removal of an inquiry, choose “Privacy request” on the contact form and include its receipt reference, without adding unnecessary sensitive documents."]
 ]},
 terms:{title:"Information first.\nProject terms, separately.",intro:"The website presents equipment information and accepts project inquiries. It does not provide an online checkout or automatically place an order.",sections:[
  ["purpose","Purpose of this website","Product pages explain the portable light pole lifter and the information needed for a configuration review. Submitting a form creates an inquiry record. It is not a purchase order, a reservation or confirmation that the equipment is suitable for a specific site."],
  ["specifications","Specifications and suitability","The published product specifications refer to the supplied specification sheet. The actual assembled pole, flange, anchor bolts, foundation and site conditions require review. Listed bolt compatibility does not establish which components are included; the standard configuration is described separately on the product page."],
  ["performance","Performance information","Lifting time, lifts per full charge and usage count are manufacturer-reported figures. Field conditions and results are still being documented. These figures do not establish total installation time, a guaranteed service life or a project saving."],
  ["commercial","Commercial arrangements","Configuration, delivery arrangements and other commercial terms are discussed privately for the project. No automated order acceptance, transaction processing or payment collection takes place on this website. Any actual supply arrangement needs its own agreed documentation."],
  ["operation","Use of technical information","The compatibility guide prepares information for review. It is not an operating procedure or engineering approval. Site operation, anchoring and safe working arrangements need reviewed instructions and competent project assessment; unresolved wording in a source sheet must not be treated as a finished operating manual."],
  ["submissions","Your submission","Send accurate contact information and only drawings or files you are authorised to share. Keep the receipt reference if the form confirms submission. If confirmation is not shown, the interface will not claim the inquiry was received; you may retry with your details still in the form."]
 ]},
 editorial:{title:"Know what\nthe information supports.",intro:"Our product information separates source-sheet facts, reported performance and evidence that still needs to be completed.",sections:[
  ["sources","The current product source","The product specification sheet supplied and confirmed for this equipment is the current source for listed dimensions, weights, battery voltage, rated load and included components. The public brand is volvet. Historical templates, research estimates and old marketing copy do not override those facts."],
  ["facts","Specifications and configuration","Dimensions and units are checked for consistency. In particular, the source lists a 300 kg rated load; it is not described as 600 lb. The M24 size appears in the compatibility table, while the standard included list names M16, M18, M20 and M22. These distinctions are preserved in the content."],
  ["claims","Reported performance","The sheet's lifting time, full-charge lift count and usage count are labelled as manufacturer-reported. They are not presented as completed field tests. A field report would need the load, attachments, foundation, conditions, timing method and original records."],
  ["limits","Engineering questions","Where the flange diagram or operating wording needs clarification, the website asks for project drawings and review. It does not expand ambiguous source wording into installation instructions. A matching height or bolt label alone does not create a compatibility verdict."],
  ["evidence","Cases, certificates and media","Customer cases and certificates need supporting material before they can be used as evidence. Product reference images explain the equipment; they are not installation-test footage. Public industry projects are not represented as volvet customers without project evidence and permission."],
  ["corrections","Updates and corrections","The content baseline is dated 28 October 2026. Changes to product facts should be checked against the source and applied to page text, specifications and structured data together. You can flag a possible error through the support option on the contact form."]
 ]}
};
const p=pages[kind];
---
<main id="main"><div class="wrap"><p class="breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a> / {kind==="editorial"?"Information policy":kind==="privacy"?"Privacy":"Terms"}</p><div class="page-intro"><p class="eyebrow">volvet / 28 October 2026</p><h1 style="white-space:pre-line">{p.title}</h1><p class="lead muted">{p.intro}</p></div><div class="policy-layout"><aside aria-label="On this page">{p.sections.map(([id,title])=><a href={`#${id}`}>{title}</a>)}<a href="/contact-us/?inquiryType=privacy">Send a request ↗</a></aside><article class="policy-body">{p.sections.map(([id,title,body])=><section id={id}><h2>{title}</h2><p>{body}</p></section>)}<p class="note">For project communication, use the <a href="/contact-us/">contact form</a>. Direct email, phone and corporate contact identity remain pending configuration.</p></article></div></div></main>
